This file describes how to build Airoha ATF from sources.

REQUIREMENTS:
 * Airoha AN7581/AN7583 SDK (2025Q1 or newer)
 * Airoha EN7523 SDK (for en7523 builds only)

1) Build Airoha SDK. The following utility is required

    * trx-airoha -- airoha specific trx utility

2) In the EN7523 SoC case

   * Create 'plat/ecnt/blobs/en7523' directory

   * Fill 'plat/ecnt/blobs/en7523' directory with the files from
     Airoha EN7523 SDK. The following file structure MUST be created:

        /"
        +-- bl1.bin"
        +-- bl22"
        |     +-- dramc.o"
        |     +-- dramc_pi_basic_api.o"
        |     +-- dramc_pi_calibration_api.o"
        |     +-- dramc_pi_main.o"
        |     +-- efuse_load.o"
        |     +-- efuse.o"
        |     +-- hal_io.o"
        +-- bl23"
        |     +-- cortex_a53.o"
        |     +-- ecnt_npu_img.o"
        |     +-- efuse_load.o"
        |     +-- efuse.o"
        +-- bl31.bin"

     bl1.bin, bl31.bin     -- take files from directory
                              ${SDK32}/airoha_feeds/package/airoha/bootloader/bootloader/unopen_img/${profile}/atf

     dramc.o, cortex_a53.o -- take files from directory
                              ${SDK32}/airoha_feeds/package/airoha/bootloader/bootloader/unopen_img/${profile}/atf/bl2

     other object files    -- extract from archieve
                              ${SDK32}/airoha_feeds/package/airoha/bootloader/bootloader/unopen_img/${profile}/atf/bl2/libbl2.a

3) Prepare building directory with the following command

     ${this_repo_path}/scripts/build-prepare.sh

4) Enter to the build directory

     cd atf-airoha-build/build

5) If necessary, edit build-${SOC}.sh scripts to tune your build options

   You may need to tune following options

     * OPTEE                               -- enable optee
     * OVERRIDE_UBI_START_ADDR             -- where to find UBI spi-nand partition
     * TCSUPPORT_GPT_ATF_SUPPORT           -- search for fip image in GPT 'fip' partition
     * OVERRIDE_PLAT_ECNT_BL31_FIP_OFFSET  -- read fip image from specified eMMC offset
                                              if TCSUPPORT_GPT_ATF_SUPPORT is not set
                                              or GPT 'fip' partition was not found

   Current settings are:
     * OPTEE=no
     * OVERRIDE_UBI_START_ADDR=0x100000
     * TCSUPPORT_GPT_ATF_SUPPORT -- enabled
     * OVERRIDE_PLAT_ECNT_BL31_FIP_OFFSET=0x84000

   OpenWrt compatible settings are:
     * optee -- disabled
     * OVERRIDE_UBI_START_ADDR=0x20000
     * TCSUPPORT_GPT_ATF_SUPPORT is not set
     * OVERRIDE_PLAT_ECNT_BL31_FIP_OFFSET is not set or OVERRIDE_PLAT_ECNT_BL31_FIP_OFFSET=0x20000

   Please fix in the script all places where these defines are mentioned.

   WARNING: OpenWRT settings are incompatible with spi-nand flashes that
            have 256 KB erase block.

6) Build ATF images

      $ ./build-${SOC}.sh

   resulting images will be stored in

     out/${SOC}/

   directory

7) You may also run 'build-flash-images.sh' to create ready to flash ATF images

8) Have fun!
